      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am bit puzzled on why this is needed.\n\nIf you notice at L264 and. L279. the instances of `sshModule` and `httpModule` classes are created through a `sysInjector.getInstance()` which means that the Guice `Injector` object of the modules will be `sysInjector`.\n\nThe above are explicitly binding the `sshModule` and `httpModule` to the same `sysInjector`, which is also assured here below.\n\nHowever, I you want to make sure that the `sshModule` and `httpModule` are *NOT* actually bound to the potentially hierarchical `sysInjector` but rather to the top-level `baseInjector`. Then it would make sense to just instantiate the `sshModule` and `httpModule` in this if() condition rather than checking again from L257 onwards.",
