      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e If you notice at L264 and. L279. the instances of `sshModule` and `httpModule` classes are created through a `sysInjector.getInstance()` which means that the Guice `Injector` object of the modules will be `sysInjector`.\n\nSadly, that\u0027s not true and that\u0027s the whole problem. Guice will by default bind to the higher parent, the baseInjector in this case, and not to the sysInjector like you would expect based on `sysInjector.getInstance()`. You **must** have the `bind()` calls to force that binding to the sysInjector. It\u0027s the whole reason this change is needed. I explained this more in L33-39 of this change\u0027s commit message and also in the original pre-revert [commit message](https://gerrit-review.googlesource.com/c/gerrit/+/417915/5//COMMIT_MSG).",
      "parentUuid": "099307b9_8f24419a",
